COMMENT ON COLUMN property_event.event_type IS 'What happened. One of CREATED_SEALED, SEAL_CHANGED, CONTAINER_TYPE_CHANGE, MOVED, TRANSFERRED, RECEIVED, RETURNED, DISPOSAL_REQUIRED, DISPOSED, COMBINED, CREATED_IN_ERROR, REMOVED, REACTIVATED, LOCATION_CONFIRMED, or the five driven by prisoner movements - PRISONER_TRANSFERRED_OUT, PRISONER_RECEIVED, PRISONER_RELEASED, DIED_IN_CUSTODY, PRISONER_ADMITTED. RECEIVED confirms arrival of the existing container at another establishment, recording the user, time, sending and receiving prisons, seal and location. Each type implies a status. [Example: SEAL_CHANGED] [SAR: Y] [Sensitivity: NONE]';

COMMENT ON COLUMN property_container.prison_id IS 'Agency (prison) this container record is assigned to. On transfer out it remains the sending prison until arrival is recorded. If the receiving establishment logs receipt in place, this record is reassigned there; if it creates a separate record, this record remains assigned to the sending prison and is linked to the new one. Read with prisoner_number it indicates where that prisoner''s property is, and normally where the prisoner is. [Example: LEI] [SAR: Y] [Sensitivity: PERSONAL]';

COMMENT ON COLUMN property_event.to_prison_id IS 'Destination agency (prison) associated with this event; null when the event has no destination. On CREATED_SEALED it identifies the establishment where the record was created; on TRANSFERRED it is the sending establishment''s expected destination; on PRISONER_RECEIVED or PRISONER_ADMITTED it identifies where the prisoner arrived and the property is due to follow; on RECEIVED it records the establishment that received this container in place. The meaning depends on event_type. [Example: MDI] [SAR: Y] [Sensitivity: PERSONAL]';
